spes: en1, the interface for mobile data, draft (0211; modem_cell=1, test without modem: modem_cell=2 modem_cell_test=1).

bsd/dev/spes_cell.c (draft, docs/SPES-CELL-DRAFT.md) after HackiOS hakios.cell.c: an Ethernet-looking en1 with a made-up
locally administered MAC and router; ARP answered for every address but our own, a minimal DHCP server (OFFER/ACK with
mask, router, DNS, lease, MTU) answered locally, so configd sets en1 up like a USB Ethernet adapter. TX: IPv4 without the
Ethernet header to spes_ipa_tx (0210); RX via spes_ipa_rx_hook, wrapped and fed to ifnet_input. Session from the QMI side
through spes_cell_set_session() (host order; not wired yet). Started from SpesModem's thread after spes_ipa_init();
nothing without the boot-arg. modem_cell=2 modem_cell_test=1 gives a fake session to test configd/DHCP alone.

